{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/37810-the-hobbit-and-the-hedge","id":37810,"title":"The Hobbit and the Hedge","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-27T05:59:37-08:00","id":37810,"title":"The Hobbit and the Hedge","content":"So, I was watching the Desolation of Smaug, and one thing that struck me pretty strongly is that Mirkwood was basically exactly how I tend to imagine the Hedge. Weird, full of illusions, a narrow, winding path through a gnarled and thorny undergrowth, and lots of unusual dangers. There were elements from the books as well that didn't make it into the movie (the stream that put people to sleep, for example) that would also make pretty interesting elements to the Hedge.<br /> <br /> It's not really surprising I guess, given the feel of the Hobbit is so very close to that of a fairy tale in the first place. It has led me to considering how many elements I could pull out of the Hobbit wholesale for use in my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T07:50:33-08:00","id":37857,"title":"","content":"Oh I agree! In the book, the elves were pretty nasty too, as they were happy to let wanderers starve or die of thirst rather than help them out. The closeness and oppression of the forest works quite well for the Hedge as well. <br /> <br /> On the subject of Mirkwood:<br /> <br /> Tolkien derived the name and concept from <b>Myrkvi\u00f0r</b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"> from Norse Mythology. Though this was a general term that likely referred to any large, unmapped forest, it also was referenced as a barrier between worlds. In the </span></span>Lokasenna (Lokis quarrels) section of the Poetic Edda, Mirkwood was between Asgard and Muspelheim (realm of the fire giants). <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T16:39:53-08:00","id":38062,"title":"","content":"Yeah I was going to say Murkwood is the Iron Woods of Norse Mythology filled with Trolls and werewolves and the like. Like the sea, the Iron Woods connected to multiple realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T14:07:51-08:00","id":38872,"title":"","content":"Heh, now I can't help but imagine that the Hobbit is actually the origin story of how Dzarumazh ended up with a sliver of iron next to his heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-02T17:43:54-08:00","id":41419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/37810-the-hobbit-and-the-hedge?p=38872#post38872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heh, now I can't help but imagine that the Hobbit is actually the origin story of how Dzarumazh ended up with a sliver of iron next to his heart.</div> </div> </div> </div> And now I imagine a loyalist Inventor making a token like Iron Man's power core for Dzarumazh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1249-yawgmoth","name":"Yawgmoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":